stateDiagram-v2
    state "ACTIVE" as active
    state "RETIRED" as retired

    [*] --> active: first explicit Base save creates account preference
    active --> retired: Base reset / locked actor setting transaction
    retired --> [*]: historical account preference retained

    note right of active
      ClientPreferenceStatus target IDs are ACTIVE=0
      and RETIRED=1. Visa reads only explicit display
      children from this account row and applies them
      to the matching anonymous AppPreference. It never
      creates an account row during sign-in.
    end note

    note right of retired
      A later explicit save creates a new active row;
      this row is not reactivated. Legacy explicit_fields
      provenance is not inferred. The schema cutover
      migration is authored but unapproved and unapplied.
    end note
